napi_enable(&lan966x->napi);
kfree(old_pages);

Reason:
The fix saves the old page array before any freeing. The call to `lan966x_fdma_rx_free_pages()` is removed entirely, so old pages remain valid until after the new allocation succeeds. On the success path, the saved old pages are freed via the page pool and the old page pool is destroyed – preventing leaks. On the failure (restore) path, the old descriptors, pages, and page pool are still intact, so restoring them is safe. The restore path also now re-enables NAPI and wakes the netdev, matching the success path and ensuring normal operation resumes. The saved old_pages array is freed in both cases with `kfree(old_pages)`.

